			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1980701">
									

<p>I'm sorry, Kalinin. I didn't keep a written record of who I talked to each time so I wasn't able to give proper thanks (note for next time). You were the one that first pointed out The Jaunt to me as well, right?</p>
<p>In any case, I definitely took your earlier criticism to heart and I made a number of changes to the draft to try and address the concerns. I think the scip is a *lot* better for having had your input.<br />
- Lowered the time frame of the coverup from X number of years to ~4 months<br />
- Cut the number of prisoners to 1/4 of what it was initially<br />
- Made it explicit that he was actively bribing inquirers that he couldn't delay otherwise<br />
- Made it explicit that he put the entire place into lockdown before moving people.<br />
- Had him do nearly all of the moving after he had starved the prisoners.</p>
<p>I realize that there is an inherent &quot;ask&quot; of the reader about the plausibility of the character doing it all alone, but when I wrote up a version where he had help, I thought it hurt the story even more.</p>
<p>I wish I could find a way to write it in a way that let you suspend disbelief. I genuinely tried to give sufficient rationale to justify the story I wanted to tell, but it appears I didn't succeed in your case. Hopefully, my next attempt will be more up your alley.</p>

